(1907100, 258293, 35545, '<td valign="top">I agree with Dr. Achoo -- your colors are flat and the piece of equipment doesn''t stand out from the background.  I was going to say that maybe if you had fooled around with depth of field, but then I noticed that you shot it at F2.8.<br/> <br/>I don''t know if you have access to Photoshop or a similar program, but it looks as if this is pretty much as it came out of the camera.  I''d try pumping up the colors some, increasing the contrast, or maybe converting it to black and white.<br/> <br/>I recognized the piece of equipment immediately.  Too bad you couldn''t have had Jane Fonda posing for you.<br/> <br/>Keep on shooting.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I agree with Dr. Achoo -- your colors are flat and the piece of equipment doesn''t stand out from the background.  I was going to say that maybe if you had fooled around with depth of field, but then I noticed that you shot it at F2.8. I don''t know if you have access to Photoshop or a similar program, but it looks as if this is pretty much as it came out of the camera.  I''d try pumping up the colors some, increasing the contrast, or maybe converting it to black and white. I recognized the piece of equipment immediately.  Too bad you couldn''t have had Jane Fonda posing for you. Keep on shooting. ', '2005-11-30 09:18:45.000000', NULL, 0),
