(1929472, 260509, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I have to say I love animal shots and this was a great one.  Congrats on the top 20.  Pair of Predators was prefect for the even category in my opinion.  We obviously have an even number of subjects, they fill the field excellently.  The colors are nice and warm, making the animals look so peaceful.  I like how you cropped the image nothing too tight or too open.  The only thing I would have not done is the border, but that''s just me and it didn''t take away from the score I gave you (10).</td>', '*Critique Club* I have to say I love animal shots and this was a great one.  Congrats on the top 20.  Pair of Predators was prefect for the even category in my opinion.  We obviously have an even number of subjects, they fill the field excellently.  The colors are nice and warm, making the animals look so peaceful.  I like how you cropped the image nothing too tight or too open.  The only thing I would have not done is the border, but that''s just me and it didn''t take away from the score I gave you (10).', '2005-12-06 22:52:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1929565, 260548, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>This is a very elegant looking image.  Burgundy for Two is a prefect fit within the even category.   Pretty decent placement in the top 30. I love the coloring and warm glow from the backdrop drawing the viewers into the subjects.  I would be curious to see the shot with a tighter crop.  Of course I guess it might harm the background more if you cropped it too tight.  The glasses seem to be an excellent choice especially since there are no spots, like you sometimes see on other shots. I really like what you did and I think the voters agree.  Good job!</td>', '*Critique Club* This is a very elegant looking image.  Burgundy for Two is a prefect fit within the even category.   Pretty decent placement in the top 30. I love the coloring and warm glow from the backdrop drawing the viewers into the subjects.  I would be curious to see the shot with a tighter crop.  Of course I guess it might harm the background more if you cropped it too tight.  The glasses seem to be an excellent choice especially since there are no spots, like you sometimes see on other shots. I really like what you did and I think the voters agree.  Good job!', '2005-12-06 23:21:39.000000', NULL, 0),
